{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1458030-how-often-do-you-use-enemies-with-weapons","id":1458030,"title":"How often do you use enemies with weapons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-30T00:54:56-07:00","id":1458030,"title":"How often do you use enemies with weapons?","content":"Hello all, I was just wondering how often you use villains or minions with weapons? I have noticed that I seem to use a lot of &quot;unarmed&quot; monsters and creepy stuff rather than artifact or mortal weapon swinging bad guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T01:31:43-07:00","id":1458037,"title":"","content":"Lots? Most of my bad guys are humans. Most of my humans use weapons.<br /> <br /> Monsters are great for slugging it out with the Exalted because they're powerful. But there tends to be very little conflict.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why shouldn't we Full Excellency dice and slice the behemoth?&quot;<br /> &quot;We kill the demon, pull out its bones to make artifacts, and are celebrated as heroes!&quot;<br /> <br /> Human opposition might fold like a house of cards, but generally gives the players a reason not to go all-out-murder-hobo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T10:38:23-07:00","id":1458066,"title":"","content":"Fairly commonplace. Monsters may fight with tooth and claw, but men forge fangs and hide made of steel or fallen beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T11:13:56-07:00","id":1458069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1458030-how-often-do-you-use-enemies-with-weapons?p=1458037#post1458037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots? Most of my bad guys are humans. Most of my humans use weapons.<br /> <br /> Monsters are great for slugging it out with the Exalted because they're powerful. But there tends to be very little conflict.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why shouldn't we Full Excellency dice and slice the behemoth?&quot;<br /> &quot;We kill the demon, pull out its bones to make artifacts, and are celebrated as heroes!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That i ocasionally play with by throwing a creature that spurts something dangerous or sprouts extra limbs/heads/doubles when cut, a monster that is capable of communication or beloved of a group of mortals for some reason or other (&quot;Leave Fae-Eating Cocaine Hippo alone!!!!&quot;), just for complications &amp; variety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1458030-how-often-do-you-use-enemies-with-weapons?p=1458037#post1458037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human opposition might fold like a house of cards, but generally gives the players a reason not to go all-out-murder-hobo.</div> </div> </div> </div>With human, beastmen and other people in the &quot;fragile puny mortals&quot; category, having weapons can serve to <i>disincentive </i>a fight, as intimidation factor and visual remainder of the potential consequences of going all out instead of talking, at least for some, so having them around is pretty useful even if you <b>don't</b> want to a melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}